       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like it might be a mistake.\n\n**Why:** 1600 mg four times daily adds up to **6400 mg/day**. For adult ibuprofen by mouth:\n- The usual maximum single dose is **800 mg**.\n- The usual maximum daily dose is **3200 mg/day**, and that's for prescription use under supervision.\n\nSo each dose would be twice the usual maximum, and the daily total would also be twice the maximum. That raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and other harm, even with normal organ function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **400 mg four times daily** (1600 mg/day). This is a common anti-inflammatory/pain dose, and 1600 mg may have been meant as the daily total.\n2. **800 mg three times daily** (2400 mg/day).\n3. **800 mg four times daily** (3200 mg/day). This is the maximum daily dose.\n4. Something else. Tell me the dose and how often.\n\nLet me know which one you want and I'll enter it. If you really do mean 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a reason, and I'll add it as a note on the order. A pharmacist would probably still need to review it."
      }
